.\" SayItErmano manual page — sayit-ermano(1).
.\" Written from the REAL CLI: `sayit-ermano --help` and every
.\" subcommand's `--help` (tests/test_deb_lock.py pins the subcommand
.\" coverage against the argparse parser, so this page cannot drift
.\" silently). File locations come from fluidvoice/paths.py.
.\"
.\" Rendering check: groff -man -ww -Kutf8 docs/man/sayit-ermano.1
.TH SAYIT\-ERMANO 1 "2026-11-23" "SayItErmano 0.9.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sayit\-ermano \- local voice dictation with AI polish
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sayit\-ermano
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS ]
.sp
.B sayit\-ermano \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
SayItErmano is a community Linux port of FluidVoice: press a global
hotkey anywhere, speak, and the transcription is typed into the focused
application. Recognition runs on-device with Whisper (faster-whisper
int8, CUDA when available); an optional AI polish pass via any
OpenAI\-compatible endpoint cleans up filler and punctuation before
insertion. Spoken punctuation commands are supported.
.PP
The daemon
.RB ( sayit\-ermano\  daemon )
owns the hotkey, the microphone and the model; a native GTK app
.RB ( sayit\-ermano\  app )
provides History and Settings windows. Everything runs locally; the
network is used only for the first-run model download, the optional AI
polish endpoint and the release update check.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show the help message and exit
.TP
.B \-\-version
show the program version and exit
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BI daemon " [\-\-no\-hotkey] [\-\-no\-sounds] [\-\-config FILE]"
run the dictation daemon in the foreground.
.B \-\-no\-hotkey
skips the X11 global hotkey (bind
.B "sayit\-ermano toggle"
instead),
.B \-\-no\-sounds
disables the start/stop sounds.
.TP
.BI toggle " [\-\-json]"
start or stop a recording.
.TP
.BI cancel " [\-\-json]"
cancel the running recording without transcribing it.
.TP
.BI status " [\-\-json]"
show the daemon status.
.TP
.BI paste\-last " [\-\-json]"
re\-type the most recent transcription.
.TP
.BI language " [\-\-json]"
cycle the dictation language (the
.I general.language_cycle
config list).
.TP
.BI transcribe " [\-\-no\-process] [\-\-ai] [\-\-json] [\-\-out PATH] [\-\-config FILE] " FILE
one\-shot transcription of an audio file
(wav/flac/mp3/opus/oga/ogg/m4a/aac/wma/aiff/webm).
.B \-\-no\-process
skips filler/punctuation post\-processing,
.B \-\-ai
also runs AI polish,
.B \-\-json
prints structured JSON, and
.B \-\-out
writes the result to a file instead of stdout.
.TP
.BI history " [\-n N] [\-\-export PATH.zip] [\-\-scrub\-tests] [\-\-yes]"
show the
.I N
most recent transcriptions.
.B \-\-export
writes history plus retained audio to a zip;
.B \-\-scrub\-tests
removes test\-suite fingerprint rows (dry\-run by default,
.B \-\-yes
applies after writing a backup).
.TP
.BI config " [path|init|print]"
show the config file path (default), write a starter config
.RB ( init ),
or print the active configuration
.RB ( print ).
.TP
.B settings
open the native Settings window (alias of
.BR "app \-\-open settings" ).
.TP
.BI app " [\-\-open WINDOW] [\-\-onboard]"
open the native GTK app. WINDOW is one of
.IR history (default),
.IR settings ,
.IR general ,
.IR dictation ,
.IR models ,
.IR ai ,
.IR wayland ,
.IR about ;
.B \-\-onboard
runs the first\-run onboarding flow.
.TP
.B doctor
environment check: audio, display server, models, config \[em] run this
first when something does not work.
.TP
.BI setup " [\-\-language LANG] [\-\-model NAME] [\-y] [\-\-config FILE]"
guided first\-use setup: hardware\-grounded model recommendation,
download with progress, insertion check, verified test take.
.B \-y
accepts every default.
.TP
.B mcp
run the MCP server on stdio for MCP\-capable agents (forwards to the
running daemon).
.TP
.BI eval\-run " SUBCOMMAND ..."
local evaluation harness
.RI ( run / check / fixtures / soak );
flags are passed through.
.TP
.BI update " [\-\-dismiss] [\-\-json]"
check for a newer release and print the upgrade command for this
install (nothing is executed).
.B \-\-dismiss
stops the update notification for the current release.
.TP
.BI license " [KEY]"
import a license key from your purchase email, or show the current
license status when KEY is omitted.
.SH FILES
All locations honor the XDG environment variables; the defaults below
assume they are unset. A pre\-rename
.I fluidvoice
directory is taken over (renamed) once on first run.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sayit\-ermano/config.toml
user configuration (created by
.BR "config init" ;
override with
.B SAYITERMANO_CONFIG
or
.BR \-\-config ).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sayit\-ermano/history.jsonl
transcription history (one JSON row per take).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/sayit\-ermano/audio/
retained per\-take audio (when retention is enabled).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/sayit\-ermano/models/
downloaded speech models.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sayit\-ermano.sock
control socket the CLI talks to (override with
.BR SAYITERMANO_SOCKET ).
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Run
.B sayit\-ermano doctor
for an end\-to\-end environment check. The daemon logs to stderr; under
the systemd user unit read them with
.BR "journalctl \-\-user \-u sayit\-ermano.service" ,
otherwise they land in the session's stderr (e.g. the XDG autostart
log).
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/acailic/SayItErmano/issues
the issue tracker
.UE .
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation ships with the source repository and the release
